   fourcouncilor_trigger_lich = "lich"
   fourcouncilor_trigger_marion = "marion"
   fourcouncilor_trigger_ohm = "ohm"
   fourcouncilor_trigger_princess = "princess"
   fourcouncilor_trigger_tendrath = "tendrath"
   fourcouncilor_trigger_token = "token"
   fourcouncilor_trigger_token_2 = "token"
   fourcouncilor_trigger_tos = "tos"
   fourcouncilor_trigger_venya_cyr = "venya'cyr"
   fourcouncilor_trigger_zarrus = "zarrus"

   // OneCouncilor (Alzahakar)
   onecouncilor_speech_001 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"The necromancer amulet is worn by those who serve "
      "the Lich directly. They are a mouth through which the Lich can feed. "
      "All who are slain by the hand of a necromancer sate the Lich's "
      "hunger.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_002 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Barloque is an exquisite city. In my days as a "
      "fledgling wizard, I maintained residence within her grand walls. It "
      "was expensive, but my mastery of magic allowed me with means by which "
      "to live there.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_003 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"It was to be the greatest seat of culture that "
      "the meridian had ever known.  They were a strong, organized peoples "
      "who suffered from self-righteousness and nobility.  Very dangerous "
      "for a city.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_004 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"May the gods see no reason to destroy you.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_005 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"How many nights did I burn a candle to the base "
      "studying at the University in Cor Noth? The scholarly atmosphere was "
      "most conducive to higher learning.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_006 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"The King has personally appointed me, his oldest "
      "friend and ally, as the head of the council of five. Together we will "
      "break the secrets of the tokens and perhaps use them to mend the "
      "ancient Meridian.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_007 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I find that I am torn when placing my vote. "
      "Akardius is new, yet quite capable.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_008 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"The ancient Nexus of power connected this land to "
      "the former empire. Long ago, the Nexus snapped and nearly destroyed "
      "this world. The five tokens are the magical key to reconstructing the "
      "nexus. However, the theoretical new Nexus would not necessarily "
      "connect back to the empire of old. Who can truly say what could be in "
      "store for us?\""
   onecouncilor_speech_009 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"The spells of some disciplines require dedication "
      "to certain moral alignments. The fey are useful in changing that "
      "alignment quickly. \""
   onecouncilor_speech_010 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Greetings, my little friend.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_011 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"They are children of the mage Tendrath. Their "
      "swords grant them great powers, but also demand a sacrifice that "
      "seems brutal to some.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_012 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"The hunters have sworn eternal vengeance on the "
      "necromancers and all those who spill the blood of the innocent. To "
      "know that the hunters are on your heels is to know fear.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_013 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Tendrath forged the magic swords to slay the "
      "Lich. The swords were lost to the Lich when the bravest warriors set "
      "out to slay Venya'cyr but died by her powers themselves. The swords "
      "are effective against necromancers, but cannot slay the Lich.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_014 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Jasper, isn't that where Jonas led his little "
      "rebellion to?\""
   onecouncilor_speech_015 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"A misshapen man whose deformity always made his "
      "kingship suspect.  He lived in a time when people believed that the "
      "king represented the spirit of a nation.  Are things so different "
      "now?  The people did not want to see deformity.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_016 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"The Lich is the transformed soul of the ancient "
      "queen of Brax. Her name was Venya'cyr. She was seduced by the Ancient "
      "forces. They used Venya'cyr's noble ideals to corrupt her.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_017 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I believe Venya'cyr can never die. That is the "
      "curse. The more she uses these Ancient forces, the less survives of "
      "the once noble queen. Perhaps she is already completely corrupted.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_018 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Marion enjoys the protection of the goddess "
      "Shal'ille. It is a very peaceful place to study.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_019 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Ah, the fair and clever Princess Kateriina, she "
      "will one day make a beautiful queen and powerful sorceress. She is "
      "wise to spend her time in support of the magical arts.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_020 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I know little of him.  His family was killed by "
      "Venya'cyr.  It is rumored that his ghost still wanders the land.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_021 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"It is my theory that together the tokens could "
      "form a powerful bond of magic that would create the Nexus anew. Our "
      "problem is we can not seem to get them to stay in one place together "
      "long enough to invoke the proper spells and experiments. I could "
      "explain further, if you wish.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_022 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Tos has no redeeming value. Even the magic shop "
      "owner is a disgrace to the world.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_023 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"The young princess had a brother.  The brother "
      "was King of Brax. He was physically deformed and over the years he "
      "lost his voice.  The young princess was loved by the people and she "
      "performed many of the duties reserved for the king.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_024 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Once a nobleman in the House of Brax, he was the "
      "cousin of the Princess Venya'cyr.  He fled the realm for Tos when the "
      "Ancient forces guiding Venya'cyr pronounced him a rival for the "
      "throne.\""
   onecouncilor_speech_025 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Zarrus is an ancestor of the King Zarcos.  Zarrus "
      "was a cousin to Venya'cyr.  It takes no genius to figure out that the "
      "Lich, at one time, shared the bloodlines of our King.  I am sure she "
      "would like it to be thus again.\""
   onecouncilor_random_001 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"All of us on the council seek the magical tokens "
      "so that we may crack their secrets and draw from their power. I have "
      "my theories on how this magic can be utilized.\""
   onecouncilor_random_002 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"There are many magical portals open that connect "
      "areas that do not sit side by side, or even in the same dimension for "
      "that matter. Why even the underworld is known to have such portals.\""
   onecouncilor_random_003 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I am indeed a master of all magic, but the "
      "balance I must maintain is too precarious for the common wizard. You "
      "are better off staying with one school. If your mind becomes clouded "
      "with other schools, I suggest you seek the potion of forgetfulness.\""
   onecouncilor_random_004 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Beware of the magic of Riija, for little of it "
      "has any substance. Unless you believe it does, of course.\""
   onecouncilor_random_005 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"All magic comes to us directly from the gods. An "
      "atheist is impotent here in Meridian. Perhaps worse off though is "
      "someone who tries to appease all of the gods at once.\""
   onecouncilor_random_006 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I do not have time to show you how to get to the "
      "various temples, if that's what you are here to ask. Hire a "
      "mercenary, there are many that can guide the way.\""
   onecouncilor_random_007 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I have theories on how the tokens function in "
      "this dimension and how they can be used in the future.\""
   onecouncilor_random_008 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Priestesses are not the only ones who can teach "
      "magic to those willing to learn.\""
   onecouncilor_random_009 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Many people wonder if we still have a king. "
      "Indeed, it is so. I, and I alone, speak to him frequently. His "
      "highness is... too preoccupied with his studies to be burdened by "
      "company or the kingdom.\""
   onecouncilor_random_010 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I can not believe how many minor magicians walk "
      "with the pride of a full sorcerer. I pity them should they cross my "
      "path.\""
   onecouncilor_random_011 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I do not traffic with the other council members "
      "very much. They are not to my tastes, except perhaps Esseldi. At "
      "least he has the sense to track down the Mana Nodes. He also has some "
      "interesting theories on the Tokens.\""
   onecouncilor_random_012 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Do not put any stock in that wasted wizard "
      "Maleval. He is a charlatan, nothing more.\""
   onecouncilor_random_013 = \
      "~kStrangely, the fireplace does not seem to give off as much heat as "
      "you would expect."
   onecouncilor_random_014 = \
      "~kAlzahakar makes a mystical gesture. You are unsure of what magic he "
      "may have just cast."
   onecouncilor_random_015 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Please, warm yourself by my fire.\""
   onecouncilor_random_016 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I sense a peacefulness in the continuum. All is "
      "well.\""
   onecouncilor_random_017 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Clearly Shal'ille's magic ranks stronger than "
      "that of the other gods.\""
   onecouncilor_random_018 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"How serene the world seems when you fully devote "
      "yourself to the goddess Shal'ille.\""
   onecouncilor_random_019 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"The spirit of Shal'ille is with us. A most "
      "blessed occurrence.\""
   onecouncilor_random_020 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Do not underestimate the raw power of Faren. I've "
      "seen many a lesser sorcerer consumed by his own spells when "
      "carelessly cast.\""
   onecouncilor_random_021 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Kraanan is not just a warrior's god. No, his "
      "magic is quite potent in directly combating other spells.\""
   onecouncilor_random_022 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"Being a practitioner of all magics, I find the "
      "fey of the Vale of Sorrows particularly useful.\""
   onecouncilor_random_023 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I find Qor's magic to be most potent, don't you? "
      "You should master it, her dark shadows are most inviting.\""
   onecouncilor_random_024 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"It is so easy to follow mistress Qor. A little "
      "blood spilled here and there, and then you can drink deeply from her "
      "power!\""
   onecouncilor_random_025 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I sense the forces of evil strongly now. Yes, "
      "that wonderful elation that comes with black magic!\""
   onecouncilor_random_026 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I feel the dark spirits of Qor growing restless. "
      "Leave my home, else I may release them!\""
   onecouncilor_random_027 = \
      "~kAlzahakar says, \"I have some very important mystical research to "
      "do. I trust you can find the door!\""
   onecouncilor_trigger_amulet = "amulet"
   onecouncilor_trigger_barloque = "barloque"
   onecouncilor_trigger_brax = "brax"
   onecouncilor_trigger_bye = "bye"
   onecouncilor_trigger_cor_noth = "cor noth"
   onecouncilor_trigger_council = "council"
   onecouncilor_trigger_duke = "duke"
   onecouncilor_trigger_explain = "explain"
   onecouncilor_trigger_explain_2 = "explain"
   onecouncilor_trigger_fey = "fey"
   onecouncilor_trigger_hello = "hello"
   onecouncilor_trigger_hunter = "hunter"
   onecouncilor_trigger_hunter_sword = "hunter sword"
   onecouncilor_trigger_jasper = "jasper"
   onecouncilor_trigger_king_of_brax = "king of brax"
   onecouncilor_trigger_lich = "lich"
   onecouncilor_trigger_marion = "marion"
   onecouncilor_trigger_princess = "princess"
   onecouncilor_trigger_tendrath = "tendrath"
   onecouncilor_trigger_theory = "theory"
   onecouncilor_trigger_tos = "tos"
   onecouncilor_trigger_venya_cyr = "venya'cyr"
   onecouncilor_trigger_zarrus = "zarrus"

   // ThreeCouncilor (Cylill)
   threecouncilor_speech_001 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"People who rely on magic like this are vulnerable in "
      "a way that common folk are not. It would be wiser to look into the "
      "origin of their powers.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_002 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Barloque is a fairly well defended city. Its walls "
      "and moat offer excellent protection to the south, where it needed it "
      "in the old Tos wars. But her weakness is in her poorly guarded north "
      "shore. A platoon in small boats could shuttle 'round her.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_003 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"It was to be the greatest military power in the "
      "world.  The soldiers of Brax were ferocious warriors and their "
      "generals were skilled tacticians.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_004 = "~kCylill says, \"Cheerio, chap!\""
   threecouncilor_speech_005 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"A rudimentary wall surrounds Cor Noth. She has "
      "hardly any military to speak of. And her potential enemies could "
      "fully surround her. Very bad design, I say, very bad.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_006 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"My son, Cort, is the esteemed Watcher of the Arena. "
      "His mother helped him get that position. If it were up to me, he'd be "
      "going through a proper and rigid stay in the Duke's army right now.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_007 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Essentially, the council is comprised of myself and "
      "four other jolly good chaps. We look after the kingdom in the stead "
      "of King Zarcos. Most of the time my peers study these mysterious "
      "tokens. I am charged with making sure they don't fall in to the wrong "
      "hands.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_008 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"I hope Akardius can lead troops like Kalior could.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_009 = "~kCylill says, \"Ho chap!\""
   threecouncilor_speech_010 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"I fear men who have no visible leader. They can "
      "easily rise up, and then I have to deal with them. I don't fear them "
      "personally, you know, I fear the lack of leadership or of a "
      "commander.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_011 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Having once seen a hunter in action, I'm not sure "
      "there's much difference between the hunters and the necromancers.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_012 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Jasper has a good natural defense. There are only a "
      "few, very visible ways in and out. A small yet well coordinated task "
      "force could repel attackers. If war breaks out, that may be ~Ithe~I "
      "place to go.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_013 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"It was a fortress said to be built with ancient "
      "magic. The owner of that fortress was the Lich. Supposedly the castle "
      "had a labyrinth that could keep even the mightiest forces from "
      "entering its realm. Of course, the fear of the Urn alone kept most "
      "people from even trying.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_014 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Marion has the best defense of all the cities, she's "
      "protected by a goddess! I say, what could be better than a goddess "
      "who makes your enemies sheath their swords. Ha.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_015 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Qerti'nya is Cort's mother. She taught me a great "
      "deal about our lord Kraanan and about the ways of women. Probably "
      "more about the ways of women than I wished to know. She lives way out "
      "at the temple beyond the cragged mountains, which is good for her, "
      "and bloody good for me.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_016 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"The Princess believes a skilled soldier is better "
      "than a strong soldier. Fair logic, I say.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_017 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Qerti'nya is Cort's mother. She taught me a great "
      "deal about our lord Kraanan and about the ways of women. Probably "
      "more about the ways of women than I wished to know. She lives way out "
      "at the temple beyond the cragged mountains, which is good for her, "
      "and bloody good for me.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_018 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"My son, Cort, is the esteemed Watcher of the Arena. "
      "His mother helped him get that position. If it were up to me, he'd be "
      "going through a proper and rigid stay in the Duke's army right now.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_019 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Tendrath was a weak man who used his power to "
      "destroy an entire city.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_020 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Tos is protected by the capable hands of the Honor "
      "Guard. The Badlands offered superb protection to the north during the "
      "Barloque wars, but now her enemy comes from the south. It will be "
      "interesting to see if they can repel a solid siege.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_021 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"The Urn was the original source of the Lich's "
      "powers. Through the powers of this Urn, Queen Venya'cyr was "
      "corrupted.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_022 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"She was the sister of an incompetent king despised "
      "by all his people. He was weak of mind, with no experience in battle, "
      "and had neither knowledge of diplomacy nor talent for warfare.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_023 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"My son, Cort, is the esteemed Watcher of the Arena. "
      "His mother helped him get that position. If it were up to me, he'd be "
      "going through a proper and rigid stay in the Duke's army right now.\""
   threecouncilor_speech_024 = "~kCylill says, \"I know not of this man.\""
   threecouncilor_random_001 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"If you really want to know what's what about those "
      "beasties out there, you should seek Rook. That chap knows the score.\""
   threecouncilor_random_002 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"The only warrior that's worth his weight has battle "
      "scars to brag of. I wouldn't trust a man to defend my castle if he "
      "hadn't lived through a really good trouncing or two.\""
   threecouncilor_random_003 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Always remember an army or even a troupe of men is "
      "mightier than the single soldier.\""
   threecouncilor_random_004 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Keep an eye out will you for those blasted tokens. "
      "I'm in charge of protecting their safety. They are official property "
      "of the council, you know.\""
   threecouncilor_random_005 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Did I ever tell you about my underdog strategy in "
      "the battle of Ukgoth? The Nasties, or the trolls if you will, had us "
      "surrounded. We were thirty men with wounded. They numbered sixty or "
      "more. I had my men defend in a cross pattern as our five best flanked "
      "their leader. Bloody mess, all in all.\""
   threecouncilor_random_006 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"During my second tour of duty, I found myself and my "
      "men faced with ferreting out a small cult of Qor who were randomly "
      "picking off our civilians. Those buggers dug themselves so deep into "
      "the Cragged Mountains with their bloody magic, it took us near five "
      "months to give them what for.\""
   threecouncilor_random_007 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Thinking back, it was when our military exercises "
      "took us to the Druids Hills when I faced my first troll. Some of the "
      "men broke formation. A few of the chaps ran. Not I. I fought side by "
      "side with my Sergeant till the bloody beast fell. That's when I knew "
      "command was for me.\""
   threecouncilor_random_008 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"I remember when I was promoted to Captain in the "
      "Duke's Honor Guard. A small revolution had begun in Jasper. This was "
      "back 'round the time of the miner's strike. The whole place was a "
      "bloody mess with the scabs returning to the mines and what with all "
      "the riots that started up.\""
   threecouncilor_random_009 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Now if I had moved the orange footmen 'round the "
      "river to the north... that might have saved some... but then again we "
      "needed a force back for the... What? Ho? Are you still here?\""
   threecouncilor_random_010 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"You don't come by way of Tos, do you? How's my son "
      "doing there?\""
   threecouncilor_random_011 = "~kCylill says, \"Stand up straight.\""
   threecouncilor_random_012 = \
      "~kThe pleasant scent of raspberries hangs in the air near the source "
      "of the river."
   threecouncilor_random_013 = \
      "~kCylill paces back and forth, muttering something about some long "
      "ago war."
   threecouncilor_random_014 = \
      "~kCylill says, \"Jolly good day, today was, don't you think!\""
   threecouncilor_trigger_amulet = "amulet"
   threecouncilor_trigger_barloque = "barloque"
   threecouncilor_trigger_brax = "brax"
   threecouncilor_trigger_bye = "bye"
